---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = 'Write the gate';
const subtitle = 'An agent opened a PR. Pick the invariants. See which one would have caught the bug.';
---
<Base title={title} description={subtitle}>
  <article class="etude-page">
    <header class="etude-head">
      <p class="etude-kicker">Etude · Campaign Cascade · Part II</p>
      <h1 class="etude-title">{title}</h1>
      <p class="etude-relief">{subtitle}</p>
      <nav class="etude-nav">
        <a href="/etudes/campaign-cascade/">← campaign cascade etudes</a>
        <span class="etude-nav-sep">·</span>
        <a href="/puzzles/the-campaign-cascade-with-agents/">puzzle</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <section class="etude-intro">
      <p>An agent on your fleet just opened a PR. The diff looks plausible. Without a gate the operator trusts, every PR is a context-acquisition task — and the review queue eats the day.</p>
      <p>Pick the gates you want. The bug is real. See what catches it.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="etude-stage">
      <div class="etude-card">
        <p class="etude-step">Agent PR</p>
        <div class="gate-pr">
          <p class="gate-pr-title"><span class="pr-state-mini">Open</span> <code>refactor(rollup): convert Flush to fire-and-forget</code></p>
          <p class="gate-pr-meta"><strong>@agent-codemod-7</strong> · 1 file changed · +6 −9</p>
          <pre class="gate-diff"><code><span class="ctx"> func (a *Aggregator) Flush(ctx context.Context) error {</span>
<span class="ctx">     batch := a.buf.Drain()</span>
<span class="del-line">-    if err := a.sink.Write(ctx, batch); err != nil {</span>
<span class="del-line">-        return fmt.Errorf("flush: %w", err)</span>
<span class="del-line">-    }</span>
<span class="add-line">+    _ = a.sink.Write(ctx, batch)</span>
<span class="ctx">     return nil</span>
<span class="ctx"> }</span></code></pre>
        </div>

        <p class="etude-step gate-step">Pick your gates</p>
        <p class="gate-help">Choose any number. Then run the gate.</p>

        <div class="gate-list" id="gate-list">
          <label class="gate-item">
            <input type="checkbox" data-id="ci" />
            <span class="gate-name">CI suite passes</span>
            <span class="gate-desc">Test runner returns green.</span>
          </label>
          <label class="gate-item">
            <input type="checkbox" data-id="lint" />
            <span class="gate-name">Lint clean</span>
            <span class="gate-desc">No formatting / import / shadowing complaints.</span>
          </label>
          <label class="gate-item">
            <input type="checkbox" data-id="errcheck" />
            <span class="gate-name">No swallowed errors</span>
            <span class="gate-desc"><code>errcheck</code> blocks <code>_ = ...</code> on error-returning calls.</span>
          </label>
          <label class="gate-item">
            <input type="checkbox" data-id="behavior" />
            <span class="gate-name">Behavioral diff against main</span>
            <span class="gate-desc">Replay last 10K Flush calls; assert no observable change in error rate or sink writes.</span>
          </label>
          <label class="gate-item">
            <input type="checkbox" data-id="policy" />
            <span class="gate-name">Policy: refactor PRs cannot drop signatures</span>
            <span class="gate-desc">An agent PR labeled <code>refactor</code> cannot remove an error return type.</span>
          </label>
          <label class="gate-item">
            <input type="checkbox" data-id="judge" />
            <span class="gate-name">AI judge agent reviews diff</span>
            <span class="gate-desc">A coordinator agent reads the diff and the issue link; flags semantic mismatch.</span>
          </label>
        </div>

        <button type="button" id="gate-run" class="etude-next gate-run-btn">Run the gates</button>
        <button type="button" id="gate-reset" class="gate-ghost" disabled>Reset</button>

        <div id="gate-results" class="gate-results" aria-live="polite"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="etude-failure">
      <h2 class="etude-failure-title">The point</h2>
      <p>The bug is the swallowed <code>err</code>. It is invisible to CI (no test asserts on the error path), invisible to lint (the line is syntactically clean), invisible to a behavioral diff if the sink rarely fails. It is visible to <code>errcheck</code> at lint time, to a refactor-policy gate, and to a coordinator agent that reads the issue and notices a swallowed return.</p>
      <p>An operator without a quality gate they trust ends up reading every diff in the queue. The bottleneck moves from PR creation to PR review. <strong>Quality gates are the enablement artifact for the operator-as-reviewer.</strong></p>
    </section>

    <footer class="etude-coda">
      <p>The fleet writes fast. The gate writes once.</p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Base>

<script is:inline>
  const GATE_TRUTH = {
    ci:       { catches: false, why: `CI is green: no existing test asserts the error path of Flush. AI agents are particularly good at not breaking existing tests — they rarely add new ones for new behavior either.` },
    lint:     { catches: false, why: `Lint passes: <code>_ = a.sink.Write(...)</code> is syntactically clean. Default lint rulesets do not flag silently dropped error returns.` },
    errcheck: { catches: true,  why: `<code>errcheck</code> (or <code>staticcheck SA4006</code>) blocks <code>_ = err</code> on error-returning calls. <strong>Caught.</strong> One-line gate; cheapest possible.` },
    behavior: { catches: false, why: `If the sink rarely fails in production, replaying 10K Flushes shows no observable difference. The gate is sound but underpowered for low-base-rate failures.` },
    policy:   { catches: true,  why: `A refactor-labeled PR that drops an <code>error</code> return type is mechanically suspicious. The policy gate flags it without reading semantics. <strong>Caught.</strong>` },
    judge:    { catches: true,  why: `A coordinator agent reading the issue ("convert to fire-and-forget") plus the diff notices that "fire-and-forget" was scoped to the network call but the function still returns <code>error</code> for the caller's contract. Spends an Opus call to flag it. <strong>Caught.</strong>` },
  };

  const list = document.getElementById('gate-list');
  const runBtn = document.getElementById('gate-run');
  const resetBtn = document.getElementById('gate-reset');
  const results = document.getElementById('gate-results');

  runBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const picked = Array.from(list.querySelectorAll('input[type=checkbox]:checked'))
      .map(cb => cb.dataset.id);
    if (picked.length === 0) {
      results.innerHTML = `<div class="gate-verdict gate-verdict-warn"><p class="gate-verdict-label">No gates picked</p><p class="gate-verdict-text">Without any gate, the bug merges. <em>Spawn → Stall → Self-escalate → Ad-hoc merge → Cleanup.</em></p></div>`;
      runBtn.disabled = true;
      resetBtn.disabled = false;
      return;
    }
    const caught = picked.some(id => GATE_TRUTH[id].catches);
    const breakdown = picked.map(id => {
      const t = GATE_TRUTH[id];
      const v = t.catches ? 'gate-row-caught' : 'gate-row-missed';
      const verb = t.catches ? 'CAUGHT' : 'MISSED';
      const name = list.querySelector(`input[data-id=${id}]`).parentElement.querySelector('.gate-name').textContent;
      return `<div class="gate-row ${v}"><strong>${verb}</strong> · ${name}<p class="gate-row-why">${t.why}</p></div>`;
    }).join('');
    const verdict = caught
      ? `<div class="gate-verdict gate-verdict-good"><p class="gate-verdict-label">Bug caught</p><p class="gate-verdict-text">At least one of your gates blocks the merge. The operator stays out of the loop on this one.</p></div>`
      : `<div class="gate-verdict gate-verdict-bad"><p class="gate-verdict-label">Bug merged</p><p class="gate-verdict-text">None of your gates fired on the swallowed error. Welcome to the cleanup campaign.</p></div>`;
    results.innerHTML = verdict + `<div class="gate-rows">${breakdown}</div>`;
    runBtn.disabled = true;
    resetBtn.disabled = false;
  });

  resetBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    list.querySelectorAll('input[type=checkbox]').forEach(cb => { cb.checked = false; });
    results.innerHTML = '';
    runBtn.disabled = false;
    resetBtn.disabled = true;
  });
</script>

<style is:global>
  .etude-page { max-width: 38rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0; }
  .etude-head { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .etude-kicker {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: var(--label-size);
    letter-spacing: var(--label-tracking);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .etude-title { font-family: var(--serif-display); font-size: 2.25rem; line-height: 1.15; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .etude-relief { font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  .etude-nav { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .etude-nav a { color: var(--muted); text-decoration: none; }
  .etude-nav a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  .etude-nav-sep { margin: 0 0.5rem; opacity: 0.5; }

  .etude-intro { margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
  .etude-intro p { margin: 0 0 0.85rem; line-height: 1.6; }

  .etude-stage { min-height: 22rem; }
  .etude-card {
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 1.25rem;
  }
  .etude-step {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: var(--label-size);
    letter-spacing: var(--label-tracking);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .gate-step { margin-top: 1.4rem; }

  /* === PR card === */
  .gate-pr {
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 0.8rem 0.95rem 0.4rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
  }
  .gate-pr-title {
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .gate-pr-title code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    background: transparent;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .pr-state-mini {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    background: #2d7a3e;
    color: white;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 5px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .gate-pr-meta {
    margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .gate-diff {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.5rem 0;
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    overflow-x: auto;
    background: transparent;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .gate-diff code { display: block; }
  .gate-diff .ctx { display: block; padding: 0 0.5rem; color: var(--text); }
  .gate-diff .add-line { display: block; padding: 0 0.5rem; background: rgba(45, 122, 62, 0.08); color: #1a5a2e; }
  .gate-diff .del-line { display: block; padding: 0 0.5rem; background: rgba(138, 52, 32, 0.08); color: var(--accent); }

  /* === gate list === */
  .gate-help {
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .gate-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.55rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
  }
  .gate-item {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    column-gap: 0.65rem;
    align-items: start;
    padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: border-color 180ms ease, background 180ms ease;
  }
  .gate-item:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .gate-item input[type=checkbox] {
    accent-color: var(--accent);
    margin-top: 0.2rem;
  }
  .gate-name {
    grid-column: 2;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .gate-desc {
    grid-column: 2;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-top: 0.2rem;
  }
  .gate-desc code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    padding: 0.05rem 0.3rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  .etude-next.gate-run-btn {
    appearance: none; -webkit-appearance: none;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 0.65rem 1.2rem;
    border: none;
    background: var(--text);
    color: var(--bg);
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    margin-right: 0.6rem;
  }
  .etude-next.gate-run-btn:hover { background: var(--accent); }
  .etude-next.gate-run-btn:disabled { opacity: 0.55; cursor: not-allowed; background: var(--muted); }
  .gate-ghost {
    appearance: none; -webkit-appearance: none;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    padding: 0.6rem 1rem;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--muted);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .gate-ghost:hover:not(:disabled) { color: var(--text); border-color: var(--muted); }
  .gate-ghost:disabled { opacity: 0.45; cursor: not-allowed; }

  /* === results === */
  .gate-results { margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .gate-verdict {
    padding: 0.95rem 1.1rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--line);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .gate-verdict-good { border-left-color: #2d7a3e; background: rgba(45, 122, 62, 0.06); }
  .gate-verdict-bad  { border-left-color: var(--accent); background: rgba(138, 52, 32, 0.06); }
  .gate-verdict-warn { border-left-color: #d99a4a; background: rgba(217, 154, 74, 0.10); }
  .gate-verdict-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .gate-verdict-good .gate-verdict-label { color: #2d7a3e; }
  .gate-verdict-bad  .gate-verdict-label { color: var(--accent); }
  .gate-verdict-warn .gate-verdict-label { color: #8a5a1a; }
  .gate-verdict-text { margin: 0; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--text); }
  .gate-rows { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .gate-row {
    padding: 0.6rem 0.85rem;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .gate-row strong {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    margin-right: 0.5rem;
  }
  .gate-row-caught { border-left: 3px solid #2d7a3e; }
  .gate-row-caught strong { color: #2d7a3e; }
  .gate-row-missed { border-left: 3px solid var(--line); opacity: 0.85; }
  .gate-row-missed strong { color: var(--muted); }
  .gate-row-why {
    margin: 0.3rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .gate-row-why code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    padding: 0.05rem 0.3rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  /* === failure === */
  .etude-failure { margin: 2rem 0 0; padding-top: 1.25rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .etude-failure-title {
    font-family: var(--serif-display);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
  }
  .etude-failure p { line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 0.85rem; color: var(--text); }
  .etude-failure code { font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85rem; background: var(--bg-soft); padding: 0.1rem 0.35rem; border-radius: 3px; }

  .etude-coda { margin: 2rem 0 0; padding-top: 1.25rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .etude-coda p { color: var(--muted); font-style: italic; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }

  @media (max-width: 32rem) {
    .etude-title { font-size: 1.85rem; }
    .etude-card { padding: 1.15rem 1.1rem 1rem; border-radius: 10px; }
  }
</style>
